Okay, the first word is rumor.

48
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,100
Rumor.

49
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:41,660
Now this is an interesting word about gossip.

50
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:42,760
Yeah, a rumor.

51
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:46,560
So a rumor is a story that might or might not be true.

52
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:47,080
Right.

53
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:50,320
Okay, so I heard a rumor that they broke up yesterday.

54
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:55,800
Okay, so you're not sure if they broke up or no one has told you for a fact.

55
00:02:56,180 --> 00:03:02,820
No, it means I probably heard it from someone else who heard it from someone else who heard it from someone else who doesn't really know.

56
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:03,120
Right.

57
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:07,460
So rumors are maybe guesses about people and you don't know if they're true.

58
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:10,280
You see this a lot with famous people, movie stars.

59
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:14,460
They always talk about rumors that maybe they got married in secret or something.

60
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:14,840
Exactly.

61
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:18,420
There's a rumor that Angelina Jolie and Brad Pitt are breaking up.

62
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:18,680
Right.

63
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:21,140
Okay, so we don't know if it's true.

64
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:22,720
Rumor.

65
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:22,920
That's a rumor.

66
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:28,680
So now the rumor that they heard was that this girl Paula is getting a promotion.

67
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:29,980
